# Unreal Engine
# Everything here is regenerated by UnrealBuildTool from the .uproject and the
# Source tree. Committing any of it causes conflicts and bloats the repository.
Binaries/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
Build/

# Visual Studio solution and project files: regenerate with
#   dotnet <engine>/Engine/Binaries/DotNET/UnrealBuildTool/UnrealBuildTool.dll \
#     -projectfiles -project=game/Cataclysm.uproject -game -rocket -progress
*.sln
*.slnx
.vsconfig
.vs/
.idea/
*.VC.db
*.opensdf
*.sdf
*.suo

# Built lighting and reflection data for a map, written next to the .umap as
# <MapName>_BuiltData.uasset. The engine regenerates it from a lighting build, so
# it is output rather than source. This project never bakes lighting: it renders
# with Lumen, and dungeon floors are generated at run time so they cannot be baked
# at all. tools/generate_input_assets.py makes every light in the sandbox level
# Movable for that reason, so nothing should produce one of these files. The rule
# is here in case something does, because these files go through Git LFS and each
# save stores another full copy. Issue #140 has the reasoning; the same rule is in
# GitHub's own UnrealEngine.gitignore template.
#
# If a map ever does need baked lighting, add an exception for that one map rather
# than deleting this line: !game/Content/Maps/L_Whatever_BuiltData.uasset
*_BuiltData.uasset

# Unreal crash and log output
*.log
Crashes/

# A directory called dev/null holding four Git LFS hook scripts (post-checkout,
# post-commit, post-merge, pre-push). Nothing in this project puts it there on
# purpose. It appears when a git command runs with core.hooksPath set to
# /dev/null: Git for Windows resolves that to a relative path, and Git LFS
# writes its hooks into it. Any command that runs the LFS filter over a tracked
# file reinstalls the hooks, so git clone, git checkout and git add all do it in
# this repository, because *.uasset and *.umap are LFS-tracked. Issue #195 has
# the reproduction. The leading slash anchors this to the repository root so a
# real dev/ directory somewhere below is still tracked.
/dev/

